  "findings": [
    "Selected throughput improves 17.84% vs original, CI [17.08,18.60]; all blocks agree. Worker CPU/op falls 15.14%, about2.07ns, and retired instructions fall by1.",
    "Selected throughput remains29.83% below main, CI [-31.07,-28.56]. Worker CPU/op rises42.50%, about3.47ns, with58additional retired instructions.",
    "The remaining cost validates allocation before returning STATUS_BUSY for a valid uncached address. Main did not perform that validation on this path; preserving invalid-address rejection precludes blindly returning BUSY.",
    "The mask removes one alignment DIV relative to original. Counts include harness address generation/checks and are not isolated function costs.",
    "This repeated valid uncached probe is a deliberately concentrated miss-side case; production uses nonblocking reads in three mini-allocator metacursor paths, which prefetch and return WOULD_BLOCK. It is not evidence that all database reads/inserts pay this cost.",
    "All18 processes recorded thermal-counter increases over setup/warmup/measurement/cleanup, not phase-localized. The selected cycles/workerCPU proxy is lower than controls; no frequency normalization or sample exclusion was applied.",
    "Large resident/hotset rates are separate evidence and must not be pooled. This result prevents a universal claim that every cache API path is neutral versus main."
